1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,994
<i>- Previously on</i> Gotham...
- Where's Jeremiah?

2
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:06,398
(gasping)

3
00:00:08,609 --> 00:00:10,209
BRUCE: Selina, she's
not herself, Alfred.

4
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:11,607
She's desperate for revenge.

5
00:00:12,212 --> 00:00:15,046
You can't save her from herself.

6
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:17,307
NYGMA: <i>This time,
woke up on a rooftop.</i>

7
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:19,211
No idea how I got
there or what happened

8
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:20,617
<i>during the preceding hours.</i>

9
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,748
GORDON: <i>In Haven,
as long as we survive,</i>

10
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:26,025
hope survives in Gotham.

11
00:00:29,796 --> 00:00:32,163
<i>You've been promising
me help for weeks.</i>

12
00:00:32,466 --> 00:00:34,594
WALKER: <i>I'm working
on getting you help.</i>

13
00:00:35,469 --> 00:00:36,669
GORDON: I promise I won't stop

14
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:39,102
until I find those responsible.

15
00:00:40,674 --> 00:00:43,234
I've got a lead on
a guy selling RPGs.

16
00:00:43,477 --> 00:00:45,309
Oh, oh, please don't hurt me.

17
00:00:45,445 --> 00:00:48,176
I just want to
know what you saw.

18
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:50,477
You had some kind of a rocket.

19
00:00:51,351 --> 00:00:54,287
And you shot it
at that building.

20
00:01:01,695 --> 00:01:03,129
(film projector clicking)

21
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:04,697
Raise your hands, Mr. Gordon.

22
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:07,694
I'm sorry, Steve,
they made me do it.

23
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,298
All right, be quiet, you.

24
00:01:10,537 --> 00:01:12,148
Miss Zant, we're sorry
to interrupt your breakfast,

25
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:13,800
but you'll come
with us, quickly.

26
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:16,176
You may lower your
hands now, Mr. Gordon.

27
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:17,634
Turn around.

28
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:24,583
There a problem, Officer?

29
00:01:24,718 --> 00:01:27,415
We know you sold the
RPG that took out Haven.

30
00:01:28,355 --> 00:01:29,118
So?

31
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:30,815
So I want to know who bought it.

32
00:01:31,291 --> 00:01:34,659
Or what? You gonna arrest me?

33
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,261
Who said anything
about arresting you?

34
00:01:38,131 --> 00:01:39,292
I want a name.

35
00:01:40,701 --> 00:01:41,566
What do you say, boys?

36
00:01:41,702 --> 00:01:43,330
(guns cocking)

37
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:48,204
Should we show this lawman
how we feel about uninvited guests?

38
00:01:56,617 --> 00:02:01,282
Now, who told you
I sold that RPG?

39
00:02:14,334 --> 00:02:15,597
(grunting)

40
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:23,275
(gunshot)

41
00:02:40,794 --> 00:02:41,921
Eduardo?

42
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:44,292
Nice shot, right?

43
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:48,395
SOLDIER: Lower your weapon now.

44
00:02:48,535 --> 00:02:49,298
EDUARDO: Delta Force,

45
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:50,631
stand down.

46
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:53,406
What are you doing here?

47
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,875
Come on. The
last time I saw you,

48
00:02:56,209 --> 00:02:57,387
you were running
through sniper fire,

49
00:02:57,411 --> 00:02:59,539
plucking my sorry ass
from a burning truck.

50
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,800
Least I could do
was pay you back.

51
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:04,379
I had that guy right
where I wanted him.

52
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,279
I'm glad you're here.

53
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,290
Yeah, me, too.

54
00:03:11,458 --> 00:03:13,359
♪♪

55
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,457
We hated each other in boot.

56
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:21,659
Jim disapproved of my ops tempo.

57
00:03:22,269 --> 00:03:24,932
(chuckles): Yeah, 'cause you
only had one speed: too fast.

58
00:03:25,272 --> 00:03:26,749
Took me a while to
realize he wasn't afraid

59
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:28,571
to get his hands dirty.
Just being careful.

60
00:03:28,775 --> 00:03:30,607
- Yeah.
- Well,
Jim's taught me a thing or two

61
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:32,337
- about being careful.
- (laughs softly)

62
00:03:32,913 --> 00:03:34,211
So what's the mission plan?

63
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:37,680
Well, we are the help
Secretary Walker promised.

64
00:03:37,818 --> 00:03:40,583
Our goal is to make
this hellhole safe again.

65
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:42,881
So it took the murder of
hundreds of innocent civilians

66
00:03:42,923 --> 00:03:43,933
to get the government to act?

67
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:45,892
We're here to eliminate
all criminal threats.

68
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,457
We're gonna blanket
the city with flash sweeps.

69
00:03:48,595 --> 00:03:50,273
Well, what about the people
that are still trapped here?

70
00:03:50,297 --> 00:03:51,974
- They need relief now.
- Hey, I'm with you,

71
00:03:51,998 --> 00:03:53,261
but my mandate's clear:

72
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,893
first we restore order,
then we take the next steps.

73
00:03:58,004 --> 00:03:59,004
ANGEL: Sir.

74
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:01,337
We got something, sir.

75
00:04:01,475 --> 00:04:02,795
Captain Gordon,
this is my second,

76
00:04:02,876 --> 00:04:04,242
Sergeant Angel Vallelunga.

77
00:04:04,377 --> 00:04:05,377
Captain.

78
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:07,839
Ledger.

79
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:11,379
Our arms dealer kept
track of his buyers.

80
00:04:14,955 --> 00:04:16,355
"Edward Nygma.

81
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:17,690
Two RPG."

82
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:19,425
Nygma.

83
00:04:19,726 --> 00:04:21,319
Yeah, that name's on my list.

84
00:04:21,728 --> 00:04:22,821
Think he's our bomber?

85
00:04:22,963 --> 00:04:24,261
Only one way to find out.

86
00:04:24,397 --> 00:04:26,423
All right, you and
I will get Nygma.

87
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:28,596
Harvey, I need you to set up

88
00:04:28,735 --> 00:04:30,567
a command center with
the soldiers at GCPD.

89
00:04:30,871 --> 00:04:32,031
- I'll grab some guys.
- Yeah.

90
00:04:32,539 --> 00:04:33,837
Hey, look, hey, Jim.

91
00:04:34,508 --> 00:04:35,874
I'm not as fast as I used to be,

92
00:04:36,009 --> 00:04:37,375
but I still got
some fight in me.

93
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:39,604
I'm not a desk jockey.
I'm a street guy.

94
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:42,015
What you are is the
best cop that I know.

95
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:45,576
We're going after Nygma.
He's ten steps ahead.

96
00:04:45,719 --> 00:04:47,959
This thing goes sideways,
you're gonna have to take over.

97
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,450
I need your help, buddy.

98
00:04:52,926 --> 00:04:53,926
I got it.

99
00:04:57,998 --> 00:04:58,998
(door closes)

100
00:05:02,669 --> 00:05:03,728
Alfred.

101
00:05:04,771 --> 00:05:06,296
Oh, there you are, Master Bruce.

102
00:05:06,606 --> 00:05:08,939
There's been a break
in the Haven bombing.

103
00:05:09,075 --> 00:05:10,235
Seems that Gordon and Bullock

104
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:12,050
have got a rather
strong lead, apparently.

105
00:05:14,714 --> 00:05:15,794
What's the matter with you?

106
00:05:15,882 --> 00:05:17,077
I can't find Selina.

107
00:05:17,551 --> 00:05:18,951
I've looked all over
the Green Zone.

108
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,826
Somehow, I think Miss
Kyle is perfectly capable

109
00:05:21,922 --> 00:05:23,754
of looking after
herself, Master Bruce.

110
00:05:24,024 --> 00:05:25,617
Except that she's not herself.

111
00:05:26,092 --> 00:05:27,856
You saw what she
did to Jeremiah.

112
00:05:29,396 --> 00:05:30,659
Yes. I did.

113
00:05:32,766 --> 00:05:34,325
Listen, come here.

114
00:05:37,637 --> 00:05:40,004
Jeremiah Valeska
deserved to die.

115
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:43,943
Jeremiah made Selina a murderer.

116
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,745
Just like Ra's made
me a murderer.

117
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,711
Ra's goaded you

118
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,612
into stabbing him, Master Bruce.

119
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,444
He used you as an
instrument. You're no murderer.

120
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:54,649
But Selina is.

121
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:56,549
You're not the same.

122
00:05:57,624 --> 00:05:58,868
She did what she
did with open eyes,

123
00:05:58,892 --> 00:06:00,918
and you got to learn
to respect that, son.

124
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:03,491
You're wrong about her, Alfred.

125
00:06:04,831 --> 00:06:06,026
And I'm gonna go find her.

126
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:09,869
(exhales)

127
00:06:10,737 --> 00:06:12,706
(sirens wailing,
birds squawking)

128
00:06:13,807 --> 00:06:15,537
NYGMA: <i>It's Monday, 5:32 p.m.</i>

129
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:17,787
(over recorder): I'm standing
in a dumpster. My head hurts.

130
00:06:17,811 --> 00:06:19,040
(fast-forwards)

131
00:06:19,479 --> 00:06:23,382
It's happened again.
It's... Saturday, 12:16 a.m.

132
00:06:23,817 --> 00:06:25,376
My fingernails are full of dirt.

133
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:26,747
Have I been digging?

134
00:06:26,887 --> 00:06:28,583
(fast-forwards)

135
00:06:28,688 --> 00:06:30,714
I think it's Sunday. I
can't find my watch.

136
00:06:30,924 --> 00:06:33,519
And it's dark outside,
my feet are wet.

137
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:34,684
There's mud everywhere.

138
00:06:34,828 --> 00:06:35,828
God!

139
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,998
It doesn't make sense!

140
00:06:42,035 --> 00:06:44,504
You're not a murderer, Ed.

141
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:48,098
Except Kristen Kringle.

142
00:06:49,509 --> 00:06:50,772
And Officer Dougherty.

143
00:06:52,045 --> 00:06:56,449
But all those
people... and children.

144
00:06:57,183 --> 00:06:58,515
How could you do it?

145
00:06:58,785 --> 00:07:00,014
Why?!

146
00:07:00,987 --> 00:07:03,115
(panting)

147
00:07:03,456 --> 00:07:04,754
It doesn't matter why.

148
00:07:05,792 --> 00:07:06,851
What matters

149
00:07:07,827 --> 00:07:11,161
is that it was you
who killed them.

150
00:07:12,565 --> 00:07:13,692
Not me.

151
00:07:14,701 --> 00:07:15,701
(exhales)

152
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:17,136
(door thuds)

153
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,932
Edward Nygma, you're under
arrest for the attack at Haven

154
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:24,876
and the murder of
hundreds of innocent people.

155
00:07:25,011 --> 00:07:26,011
No.

156
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:28,512
No, Jim, I can explain.

157
00:07:29,215 --> 00:07:30,215
Explain?

158
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:33,478
You son of a bitch.
You actually did it?

159
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,919
- On your knees, now.
- No! I didn't.

160
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:37,856
I can prove it, I just,

161
00:07:37,991 --> 00:07:40,927
I need... I need
a little bit of time.

162
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:42,594
Say the word, Jim.

163
00:07:43,063 --> 00:07:44,063
You know me, Jim.

164
00:07:44,931 --> 00:07:46,229
The people that I...

165
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:50,133
have hurt, they hurt me first.

166
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,701
I didn't know a single
person in Haven.

167
00:07:53,106 --> 00:07:54,540
I'm innocent.

168
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:58,170
It's your call, buddy.

169
00:07:59,612 --> 00:08:01,171
He basically confessed.

170
00:08:07,053 --> 00:08:08,180
We bring him in.

171
00:08:08,722 --> 00:08:09,849
He stands trial.

172
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:11,818
Yeah, I don't think so.

173
00:08:13,526 --> 00:08:16,621
(steady beeping)

174
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,197
Your friend is standing
on a pressure-plated IED

175
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:20,932
One of several
throughout the rooms.

176
00:08:23,136 --> 00:08:27,073
Twitch, and you'll repaint
the room with your organs.

177
00:08:34,781 --> 00:08:36,079
Don't do it, Jim.

178
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:40,647
This little doohickey
monitors my heartbeat.

179
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:44,621
It increases by ten? Boom.

180
00:08:44,891 --> 00:08:46,553
Decreases by ten?

181
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:47,656
Boom.

182
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:49,005
GORDON: <i>You try
to walk out of here,</i>

183
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,349
and a special forces sniper
will put a bullet in your head.

184
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,089
No, they won't.

185
00:08:52,265 --> 00:08:54,962
This thing can detonate
his bomb from a mile away.

186
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,299
Or am I bluffing?

187
00:08:58,972 --> 00:09:01,532
Once word gets out that
you're responsible for Haven,

188
00:09:02,075 --> 00:09:03,395
you'll have a
target on your back.

189
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,101
I'll take my chances.

190
00:09:07,781 --> 00:09:08,791
(whispers): I
think he's bluffing.

191
00:09:08,815 --> 00:09:09,815
No, no.

192
00:09:09,883 --> 00:09:10,883
He doesn't bluff.

193
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:13,752
I don't want anyone here

194
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:15,531
- if this thing detonates.
- You heard the man.

195
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,114
Tell Sergeant
Vallelunga to stand down.

196
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:19,122
- Yes, sir.
- Nygma walks.

197
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:23,720
A wristband that
monitors his heart rate.

198
00:09:23,963 --> 00:09:25,056
Welcome to Gotham.

199
00:09:26,032 --> 00:09:27,193
So what we do?

200
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:30,869
Well, the way I see it,
now we're all tied up.

201
00:09:31,004 --> 00:09:32,768
I just got to save your
life one more time,

202
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:34,166
then I'm back in the lead.

203
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:37,109
Funny. Seriously, the
hell are we gonna do?

204
00:09:37,644 --> 00:09:41,342
Well, he pulled a book
to set the booby trap.

205
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:45,712
I think I can make it.

206
00:09:46,686 --> 00:09:49,656
Assuming the vibrations
don't trigger the IED, what then?

207
00:09:50,190 --> 00:09:51,021
Then we just got to figure out

208
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:52,757
what sort of puzzle
he wants us to solve.

209
00:09:53,026 --> 00:09:54,026
Puzzle?

210
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:57,221
There's always a puzzle
with Nygma. You ready?

211
00:10:12,645 --> 00:10:15,308
(beeping continues)

212
00:10:35,235 --> 00:10:36,396
(mouths)

213
00:10:37,704 --> 00:10:39,866
(exhales)

214
00:10:41,941 --> 00:10:43,967
(panting)

215
00:10:48,381 --> 00:10:52,045
<i>Chess Strategy: Knight
Moves Nimbly in the Dark.</i>

216
00:10:52,185 --> 00:10:53,813
I'm gonna wring
this nerd's neck.

217
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,687
In chess,

218
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:59,384
knights move in an "L."

219
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,285
Two spaces straight,

220
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:04,862
then one at a 90-degree angle.

221
00:11:06,966 --> 00:11:09,868
<i>Butterfly Collecting
with Conviction.</i>

222
00:11:11,938 --> 00:11:13,099
Or...

223
00:11:17,377 --> 00:11:18,902
<i>Chess Strategy:</i>

224
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,814
<i>Knight's Gambit:
Escaping Checkmate.</i>

225
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:27,719
(beeps)

226
00:11:48,808 --> 00:11:49,332
You okay?

227
00:11:49,475 --> 00:11:51,910
You left the Army for this city?

228
00:11:52,412 --> 00:11:53,412
It grows on you.

229
00:11:54,414 --> 00:11:55,414
Harvey, come in.

230
00:11:55,481 --> 00:11:57,081
BULLOCK (over radio):
Jim, you nab Nygma?

231
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:58,878
No. Put the word out:

232
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:02,087
Nygma's wanted for murder
and the attack on Haven.

233
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,487
(gunshots)

234
00:12:05,191 --> 00:12:06,391
BRUCE: <i>I'm looking for Selina.</i>

235
00:12:06,426 --> 00:12:07,426
BARBARA: <i>Follow me.</i>

236
00:12:08,962 --> 00:12:09,793
Everybody,

237
00:12:09,963 --> 00:12:12,330
raise your glasses to the killer

238
00:12:12,465 --> 00:12:14,730
of Jeremiah Valeska.

239
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:17,063
(cheering)

240
00:12:17,203 --> 00:12:19,297
(rock music playing)

241
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:22,204
CROWD (chanting):
The freak is dead!

242
00:12:22,375 --> 00:12:24,105
The freak is dead!

243
00:12:24,244 --> 00:12:27,043
The freak is dead!
The freak is dead!

244
00:12:29,015 --> 00:12:30,259
MAN (over radio):
Citizens of Gotham,

245
00:12:30,283 --> 00:12:32,809
this is a special bulletin
from the police department.

246
00:12:32,986 --> 00:12:34,506
We have identified
the person who fired

247
00:12:34,821 --> 00:12:37,450
a rocket-propelled grenade
that decimated Haven.

248
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:40,021
Be on the lookout
for a tall, skinny man

249
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:43,225
who goes by the
name of Ed Nygma.

250
00:12:43,363 --> 00:12:46,094
He was last seen wearing
a green suit and eyeglasses.

251
00:12:49,102 --> 00:12:51,970
Ed Nygma.

252
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:53,796
The monster of Haven.

253
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,180
- Let's go get him!
- ALL: Yeah!

254
00:12:55,208 --> 00:12:56,836
- Let's kill him!
- (cheering)

255
00:12:56,976 --> 00:12:58,000
Kill him!

256
00:12:58,144 --> 00:12:59,942
ALL (chanting):
Kill him! Kill him!

257
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:02,844
Kill him! Kill him! Kill him!

258
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:10,150
Excellent.

259
00:13:16,329 --> 00:13:20,130
200 bullets, as
promised. Go have fun.

260
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:21,810
And there's more
where that came from

261
00:13:21,834 --> 00:13:23,097
if you keep up the good work.

262
00:13:23,403 --> 00:13:24,837
Off you go.

263
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,338
Mr. Cobblepot, sir.

264
00:13:29,409 --> 00:13:31,344
- It's...
- What? What?

265
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:34,907
"Edward Nygma
is the monster res...

266
00:13:37,884 --> 00:13:40,820
responsible for killing
the innocents at Haven."

267
00:13:46,292 --> 00:13:48,056
(strained): Ed, what
have you done?

268
00:13:48,394 --> 00:13:50,454
I saw him go that
way! He's over there!

269
00:13:50,596 --> 00:13:52,155
Get him! Come on!

270
00:13:52,265 --> 00:13:54,029
(overlapping shouting)

271
00:14:05,878 --> 00:14:06,955
ANGEL (over radio):
Bang Zero-One.

272
00:14:06,979 --> 00:14:08,311
This is Bird Zero-Two.

273
00:14:09,315 --> 00:14:10,908
What's your status, Angel?

274
00:14:11,184 --> 00:14:12,846
ANGEL: We cleared
13th to 36th Street,

275
00:14:12,985 --> 00:14:15,978
west of Broadway. Gonna
keep pushing uptown.

276
00:14:16,589 --> 00:14:19,457
That's progress. Still no Nygma.

277
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:22,458
My boys will scoop
him up by nightfall.

278
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:27,391
Now tell me about
this... Scarecrow.

279
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,195
Well, he has chemical weapons.

280
00:14:29,335 --> 00:14:30,928
Your guys will need gas masks.

281
00:14:31,237 --> 00:14:34,207
But taking him down
would be a big win.

282
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:36,036
Well, that's why we're here.

283
00:14:45,952 --> 00:14:48,319
Psst. Hey.

284
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:58,058
(singsongy): Time to wake up.

285
00:14:58,197 --> 00:14:59,324
(gasping)

286
00:15:02,335 --> 00:15:03,132
Who are you?

287
00:15:03,269 --> 00:15:06,603
I'm the woman who's gonna
carry out your execution.

288
00:15:06,939 --> 00:15:08,100
(both whooping)

289
00:15:13,312 --> 00:15:14,312
(whooping)

290
00:15:21,621 --> 00:15:24,147
(laughter)

291
00:15:27,527 --> 00:15:29,428
(grunting, gasping)

292
00:15:33,366 --> 00:15:35,096
That's just a taste.

293
00:15:35,401 --> 00:15:39,133
It's only fair you
die slow and painful

294
00:15:39,472 --> 00:15:41,065
to pay for JoJo.

295
00:15:42,008 --> 00:15:43,067
Who's JoJo?

296
00:15:43,476 --> 00:15:46,378
JoJo was in Haven

297
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:49,981
when you blew it up.

298
00:15:51,317 --> 00:15:54,048
(laughing)

299
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,352
This is a joke, right?

300
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:02,292
300 people died in Haven.

301
00:16:02,595 --> 00:16:04,257
(scoffs)

302
00:16:04,397 --> 00:16:06,093
We don't care about people.

303
00:16:06,265 --> 00:16:08,234
- MAN: Yeah!
- (laughter)

304
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:12,336
Look at how happy JoJo was.

305
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:19,075
(crying): He always
had a smile on his face.

306
00:16:20,613 --> 00:16:23,378
You anthropomorphizing
nincompoop.

307
00:16:26,052 --> 00:16:27,748
Dogs can't smile.

308
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:34,055
- (screaming)
- (whooping)

309
00:16:34,727 --> 00:16:35,727
(shouts)

310
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:43,568
I'm going to fix you, Ed.

311
00:16:48,608 --> 00:16:49,439
What the hell?

312
00:16:49,575 --> 00:16:52,238
Floor it!

313
00:16:55,648 --> 00:16:58,584
- (whooping)
- Yeah!

314
00:17:01,587 --> 00:17:04,751
(whooping) Yeah!

315
00:17:06,792 --> 00:17:08,090
Yeah!

316
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,031
I'm going to fix you, Ed.

317
00:17:23,442 --> 00:17:24,535
Did I say stop?

318
00:17:24,677 --> 00:17:25,677
I'm sorry, Ma.

319
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,111
Ma, can't we just
beat him to death?

320
00:17:27,613 --> 00:17:28,637
(engine stalling)

321
00:17:31,784 --> 00:17:33,047
It's not starting.

322
00:17:33,185 --> 00:17:35,814
Yes. Anything but electrocution.

323
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:38,321
Please don't let
me die this way.

324
00:17:38,457 --> 00:17:41,120
Oh, thank God the
fuel line's clogged.

325
00:17:44,664 --> 00:17:47,065
Unclog the line.

326
00:17:56,208 --> 00:17:58,336
- (laughs)
- We got it, we got it. Come on.

327
00:17:58,477 --> 00:18:01,140
- (laughing)
- Please.

328
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:04,341
Shoot me, stab me,

329
00:18:04,450 --> 00:18:06,078
anything but another jolt.

330
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,452
Hit it.

331
00:18:12,358 --> 00:18:13,358
Oh, no!

332
00:18:13,693 --> 00:18:15,594
(gasping)

333
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:18,155
(screaming)

334
00:18:21,701 --> 00:18:22,701
GRETEL: Put it out!

335
00:18:22,802 --> 00:18:25,203
Boys! Oh, my Lord!

336
00:18:25,371 --> 00:18:27,363
Help him! Help him!

337
00:18:27,506 --> 00:18:29,441
(yelping)

338
00:18:31,510 --> 00:18:33,411
Who's gonna fix who, Oswald?

339
00:18:34,647 --> 00:18:37,242
HENCHMAN: The Army's invading
the city, locking everyone up.

340
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:38,550
They're coming this way.

341
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:43,249
Please. An invasion
is tanks, infantry.

342
00:18:43,689 --> 00:18:44,748
These are scouts.

343
00:18:45,691 --> 00:18:46,420
What about Nygma?

344
00:18:46,559 --> 00:18:48,537
HENCHMAN: Nobody's seen
him, but we got feelers out.

345
00:18:48,561 --> 00:18:52,555
Well, you tell your "feelers"

346
00:18:52,732 --> 00:18:54,792
that the first man
to bring me Nygma

347
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,160
is the one who gets to live.

348
00:18:58,571 --> 00:18:59,903
Now!

349
00:19:02,842 --> 00:19:04,208
(sighs)

350
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:06,704
(laughs)

351
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:10,844
I am surrounded
by morons, Edward.

352
00:19:11,183 --> 00:19:12,503
If I didn't have
an empire to run,

353
00:19:12,551 --> 00:19:15,646
I would go get Nygma
myself. (chuckles)

354
00:19:28,434 --> 00:19:29,231
(gasps)

355
00:19:29,368 --> 00:19:32,861
Hello, Oswald. We have
a great deal to talk about.

356
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,466
But first,

357
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,401
did you name your dog after me?

358
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:44,374
BULLOCK: Jim,
Harper just radioed.

359
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:46,383
She saw Nygma
going into City Hall.

360
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:47,748
He's going to Penguin.

361
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,631
EDUARDO: Cobblepot's
at the top of my list

362
00:19:49,655 --> 00:19:51,624
from Walker.
Sounds like a twofer.

363
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:52,901
GORDON: Penguin's sitting on all

364
00:19:52,925 --> 00:19:54,291
the ammo in Gotham.

365
00:19:54,427 --> 00:19:56,507
He's better defended, better
manned than anyone else.

366
00:19:58,230 --> 00:19:59,230
We need shock and awe.

367
00:19:59,465 --> 00:20:00,865
Shock and awe is my default.

368
00:20:01,701 --> 00:20:02,701
You ready?

369
00:20:05,438 --> 00:20:07,270
You know what, take
Harvey on this one.

370
00:20:07,406 --> 00:20:08,726
I'll keep things
locked down here.

371
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,267
Let's saddle up.

372
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:14,681
(rock music playing)

373
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:18,942
Man, you're killing my buzz.

374
00:20:22,321 --> 00:20:23,414
Selina.

375
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,689
I know you, and this isn't you.

376
00:20:33,499 --> 00:20:35,434
- You know me?
- Yes.

377
00:20:37,002 --> 00:20:39,335
Maybe better than
you know yourself.

378
00:20:43,442 --> 00:20:45,001
Let me tell you something.

379
00:20:47,713 --> 00:20:48,772
That night

380
00:20:49,315 --> 00:20:50,783
that your parents were murdered,

381
00:20:52,785 --> 00:20:55,311
I was in that alley

382
00:20:55,554 --> 00:20:57,352
on the fire escape.

383
00:20:59,291 --> 00:21:01,658
And I watched that guy

384
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:04,820
shoot your father

385
00:21:06,465 --> 00:21:07,956
and shoot your mother.

386
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:11,537
And through it all,

387
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:15,567
I did... nothing.

388
00:21:15,708 --> 00:21:17,438
(laughs)

389
00:21:19,545 --> 00:21:22,777
I didn't call for
help, I didn't...

390
00:21:23,849 --> 00:21:27,581
(crying): I didn't scream
for the guy to stop.

391
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:32,319
It wasn't your fault. You
were just a scared kid.

392
00:21:34,026 --> 00:21:35,494
No.

393
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:41,734
You were the scared kid.

394
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:49,666
We are not the same, Bruce.

395
00:21:53,512 --> 00:21:56,607
I didn't do anything because
I wasn't willing to risk my neck

396
00:21:56,749 --> 00:21:59,514
for someone else
because I didn't care.

397
00:22:02,021 --> 00:22:05,514
That's who I was
and that's who I am.

398
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,694
("Psycho" by Grim
Streaker playing)

399
00:22:12,731 --> 00:22:13,994
I love this song.

400
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:20,663
♪ When I want to go, I
know what you'll say... ♪

401
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:24,535
What did you do to me, Oswald?

402
00:22:25,811 --> 00:22:26,891
What are you talking about?

403
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,378
Oh, please.

404
00:22:29,515 --> 00:22:31,541
You did something to me.

405
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:33,518
You...

406
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:36,586
You are the reason

407
00:22:36,722 --> 00:22:38,418
that I killed those people.

408
00:22:38,924 --> 00:22:40,119
How could you?

409
00:22:41,093 --> 00:22:44,825
You have made me into
some murderous puppet.

410
00:22:45,731 --> 00:22:48,565
For weeks, I've been
waking up in strange places,

411
00:22:48,701 --> 00:22:51,569
not knowing how I
got there or what I did.

412
00:22:51,704 --> 00:22:53,104
Driving myself mad,

413
00:22:53,439 --> 00:22:55,135
thinking I had gone mad.

414
00:22:57,142 --> 00:22:59,543
And now I know that
it was all your doing.

415
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:02,511
Of everything

416
00:23:02,648 --> 00:23:04,514
that you have put me through,

417
00:23:07,086 --> 00:23:08,384
this...

418
00:23:09,955 --> 00:23:11,981
this is the most cruel.

419
00:23:16,528 --> 00:23:17,528
Ed.

420
00:23:18,564 --> 00:23:20,897
I don't know what
you're talking about.

421
00:23:21,734 --> 00:23:24,829
I did not make you do anything.

422
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:27,064
Then what is "I'll fix you"?

423
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:30,973
What did that mean?
You didn't fix me.

424
00:23:31,543 --> 00:23:32,704
You broke me!

425
00:23:32,912 --> 00:23:34,676
W-W-Wait. No.

426
00:23:35,547 --> 00:23:39,985
I said that to you the
night the bridges blew. I-I...

427
00:23:40,452 --> 00:23:41,715
Think I wouldn't remember?

428
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:43,988
No, Ed, I saved your life!

429
00:23:44,123 --> 00:23:45,614
That's it!

430
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:47,752
What are you talking about?

431
00:23:49,061 --> 00:23:52,657
You had been stabbed, I paid
Hugo Strange to save your life.

432
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:54,959
I bet he did something to you

433
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:56,662
when he was patching you up.

434
00:23:58,437 --> 00:23:59,928
You paid Hugo
Strange to save me?

435
00:24:01,507 --> 00:24:02,507
Why?

436
00:24:04,677 --> 00:24:06,669
What was I supposed
to do? Let you die?

437
00:24:07,646 --> 00:24:09,137
After Butch, you
were my only friend.

438
00:24:09,481 --> 00:24:10,574
You shot Butch!

439
00:24:10,783 --> 00:24:13,810
Which is why I needed you!

440
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:16,119
(shouts)

441
00:24:21,727 --> 00:24:22,922
(exhales)

442
00:24:29,835 --> 00:24:30,928
Edward Nygma,

443
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:33,901
if I wanted you to suffer,

444
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:38,977
I would never do it in
some backhanded way.

445
00:24:41,213 --> 00:24:43,773
If you and I

446
00:24:44,116 --> 00:24:46,881
are ever at odds again,

447
00:24:47,252 --> 00:24:50,711
you will know, without a doubt,

448
00:24:50,856 --> 00:24:54,725
that I am your enemy.

449
00:24:57,062 --> 00:24:59,224
I promise you that...

450
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:03,829
(crying): as a friend.

451
00:25:12,077 --> 00:25:13,136
(grunts)

452
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:15,840
(panting)

453
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:19,643
What a mess.

454
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:22,179
I might have killed you, Oswald.

455
00:25:26,625 --> 00:25:31,859
And if that day
comes... I swear to you...

456
00:25:32,931 --> 00:25:35,560
I will stare you in the eye

457
00:25:36,235 --> 00:25:38,602
as I stab you in the heart.

458
00:25:40,072 --> 00:25:41,233
(laughs softly)

459
00:25:45,811 --> 00:25:46,608
(sniffles)

460
00:25:46,745 --> 00:25:47,940
Look on the bright side.

461
00:25:48,147 --> 00:25:50,582
If Hugo Strange did
do something to you,

462
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:54,315
it means you are not
responsible for Haven.

463
00:25:57,056 --> 00:25:57,785
Where is he?

464
00:25:57,923 --> 00:25:59,892
(rumbling)

465
00:26:00,192 --> 00:26:03,287
Sir, GCPD and the Army
have blown the gates.

466
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:06,859
Stay here. You'll be safe.

467
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:10,669
(quietly): Grab Nygma.
They want him, not me.

468
00:26:12,838 --> 00:26:13,862
He's gone.

469
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:19,875
Idiot! Ugh!

470
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,876
(high-pitched whirring)

471
00:26:32,658 --> 00:26:33,658
(guns cocking)

472
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:35,227
(laughs)

473
00:26:36,929 --> 00:26:38,898
Why, hello, Harvey.

474
00:26:40,165 --> 00:26:42,828
Now, last time we
were in a standoff,

475
00:26:42,968 --> 00:26:45,369
you ran out of bullets.

476
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,364
(laughs)

477
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,975
I hope you're better prepared.

478
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,979
We don't want to take
your territory, Oswald.

479
00:26:57,683 --> 00:26:59,151
But you have to put
down your weapons

480
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:00,946
and hand over Ed Nygma.

481
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:06,058
Or, if you and your
friends aren't out

482
00:27:06,191 --> 00:27:08,285
by the time I count to three,

483
00:27:08,694 --> 00:27:11,357
I will mow you all down!

484
00:27:14,099 --> 00:27:15,099
We good?

485
00:27:15,934 --> 00:27:16,934
Yep.

486
00:27:19,371 --> 00:27:20,703
Go ahead. Count.

487
00:27:23,709 --> 00:27:25,337
(laughs)

488
00:27:25,677 --> 00:27:28,647
Harvey, you're
not thinking clearly.

489
00:27:29,348 --> 00:27:31,146
Maybe call your boss,

490
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:32,811
see what he thinks.

491
00:27:33,185 --> 00:27:35,086
I don't have to call anyone.

492
00:27:35,754 --> 00:27:38,417
Go ahead. Count.

493
00:27:50,235 --> 00:27:51,235
One...

494
00:27:53,172 --> 00:27:56,802
(panting)

495
00:28:01,146 --> 00:28:02,876
How's that for better prepared?

496
00:28:03,849 --> 00:28:05,283
Where's Ed Nygma?

497
00:28:07,786 --> 00:28:09,345
The whole of Gotham
is looking for you.

498
00:28:09,755 --> 00:28:11,849
I need information,
your specialty.

499
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:17,219
I am going to cut

500
00:28:17,362 --> 00:28:20,764
your face into a jigsaw puzzle

501
00:28:20,899 --> 00:28:22,819
and watch you try and
put it back together again.

502
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:25,463
Barbara... Barbara! Am I dumb?

503
00:28:27,206 --> 00:28:29,471
In all the years of plotting

504
00:28:29,808 --> 00:28:31,174
and the betrayals between us,

505
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:34,474
have you ever... ever...
Known me to do something

506
00:28:34,813 --> 00:28:36,333
as idiotically brutal
as shoot a rocket

507
00:28:36,415 --> 00:28:38,043
into a building full
of innocent people?

508
00:28:39,785 --> 00:28:42,778
I did not kill those
people in Haven.

509
00:28:44,756 --> 00:28:45,815
Not exactly.

510
00:28:46,959 --> 00:28:48,257
There's more going on here.

511
00:28:55,834 --> 00:28:57,132
I'm waiting.

512
00:28:59,338 --> 00:29:00,465
The night the bridges fell,

513
00:29:00,839 --> 00:29:04,799
I was hurt. Oswald took
me to Hugo Strange.

514
00:29:06,144 --> 00:29:07,772
And he did
something to my brain.

515
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:10,381
And that's your excuse for
murdering hundreds of people?

516
00:29:10,782 --> 00:29:14,378
I'm saying that
Strange, or somebody,

517
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:16,187
can control me.

518
00:29:17,222 --> 00:29:18,850
They killed those people.

519
00:29:20,892 --> 00:29:23,157
Okay, let's say, by some
miracle, I believe you.

520
00:29:23,829 --> 00:29:25,297
Why the hell should I help you?

521
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,331
Because who's
working with Strange?

522
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:31,301
Who would force me to
kill all of those people?

523
00:29:33,272 --> 00:29:35,207
Information is your lifeblood.

524
00:29:35,907 --> 00:29:40,811
You help me, and I will give
you the best intel you've ever had.

525
00:29:46,285 --> 00:29:47,981
I don't know where Strange is.

526
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:50,785
But I can tell you where
you'll find his Igors.

527
00:29:50,922 --> 00:29:51,446
(punch lands)

528
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:52,790
(grunts)

529
00:29:53,058 --> 00:29:55,220
Where is Edward Nygma?

530
00:29:57,029 --> 00:29:58,497
You're protecting
a mass murderer.

531
00:29:59,197 --> 00:30:00,460
Don't look to me for sympathy.

532
00:30:04,202 --> 00:30:05,363
Fine.

533
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:08,804
But not with that
meathead around.

534
00:30:13,111 --> 00:30:16,081
(laughs)

535
00:30:16,882 --> 00:30:19,977
You know, they say you can
judge a man by his friends.

536
00:30:20,085 --> 00:30:22,077
This from a man
who has no friends.

537
00:30:27,059 --> 00:30:28,059
Talk.

538
00:30:29,561 --> 00:30:30,995
Nygma's a patsy.

539
00:30:31,930 --> 00:30:33,421
He is not a mass murderer.

540
00:30:35,300 --> 00:30:37,394
Puzzles, games,

541
00:30:38,370 --> 00:30:42,432
perhaps the odd killing here
and there, but hundreds of people?

542
00:30:43,075 --> 00:30:46,011
No. That's not
him. You know this.

543
00:30:48,347 --> 00:30:49,872
So who set him up?

544
00:30:50,349 --> 00:30:52,250
(laughs)

545
00:30:53,352 --> 00:30:56,254
Jim, you want information,

546
00:30:56,388 --> 00:30:57,913
I want to go home.

547
00:30:58,056 --> 00:30:59,388
Eduardo's not gonna go for that.

548
00:30:59,458 --> 00:31:01,859
Oh, I'm sorry. I thought
you were in charge.

549
00:31:06,298 --> 00:31:08,028
Even if I were to let you go,

550
00:31:08,934 --> 00:31:11,335
sooner or later, the
Army's gonna come for you.

551
00:31:12,304 --> 00:31:13,636
Things are changing in Gotham.

552
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:18,241
I'll take my chances.

553
00:31:20,245 --> 00:31:21,269
Now,

554
00:31:21,413 --> 00:31:24,178
do you want Nygma or not?

555
00:31:31,123 --> 00:31:32,591
I know where Nygma's going.

556
00:31:41,166 --> 00:31:43,067
I trust you know
what you're doing.

557
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:45,570
We do what we have to do, right?

558
00:32:01,553 --> 00:32:02,553
Gentlemen.

559
00:32:02,687 --> 00:32:04,280
Come in. You're late.

560
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:10,256
The last body you procured
for me was gangrenous.

561
00:32:10,629 --> 00:32:12,621
Completely unsuitable.

562
00:32:15,967 --> 00:32:17,060
Oh, my.

563
00:32:18,136 --> 00:32:19,136
Bye.

564
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:21,262
Hello, Professor.

565
00:32:23,275 --> 00:32:24,971
(chuckles)

566
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:26,110
Mr. Nygma.

567
00:32:26,178 --> 00:32:27,355
Let's skip the part
where you deny

568
00:32:27,379 --> 00:32:28,938
making me into
a killing machine.

569
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:33,675
Tell me how you took
control of my alter ego.

570
00:32:34,686 --> 00:32:36,052
I don't follow.

571
00:32:36,455 --> 00:32:38,447
You did something to access

572
00:32:38,590 --> 00:32:40,388
the Ed Nygma side
of my personality.

573
00:32:40,559 --> 00:32:43,324
But... you're Ed Nygma.

574
00:32:43,495 --> 00:32:44,656
I'm also the Riddler!

575
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:48,057
Tell me what you did!

576
00:32:49,534 --> 00:32:51,526
Why did you make
me kill all those people

577
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:52,694
in Haven?

578
00:32:53,271 --> 00:32:54,364
You did that?

579
00:32:55,006 --> 00:32:56,167
How interesting.

580
00:32:56,675 --> 00:32:58,143
I had no idea.

581
00:32:58,276 --> 00:32:59,744
You really expect
me to believe that?

582
00:33:00,212 --> 00:33:03,011
Mr. Nygma, I don't
know anything about

583
00:33:03,148 --> 00:33:05,242
your alter egos.

584
00:33:05,484 --> 00:33:07,077
But I will confess that

585
00:33:07,352 --> 00:33:09,514
when I was sewing
up your knife wound,

586
00:33:09,654 --> 00:33:13,386
I may have tinkered a
little with your grey matter.

587
00:33:13,525 --> 00:33:16,120
- Would you just...
- I put a chip in your brain.

588
00:33:18,363 --> 00:33:21,561
It allows you to be able
to be controlled remotely.

589
00:33:23,702 --> 00:33:24,726
I knew it.

590
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:26,504
But I don't control you.

591
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:29,031
I gave control to others.

592
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:30,174
Who?

593
00:33:32,511 --> 00:33:34,173
I will write it down.

594
00:33:35,113 --> 00:33:37,139
That way, if I'm
ever confronted,

595
00:33:37,282 --> 00:33:40,377
I can honestly say
that I never told you.

596
00:33:51,763 --> 00:33:52,763
(sighs)

597
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,098
(thuds)

598
00:33:54,599 --> 00:33:56,090
Not to worry.

599
00:33:56,535 --> 00:34:00,028
You're experiencing
a simple neural cutout.

600
00:34:00,105 --> 00:34:03,166
I am mystified as to how
you've become aware

601
00:34:03,308 --> 00:34:05,300
you're being controlled.

602
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:10,311
I suppose we're just going
to have to open you up

603
00:34:10,682 --> 00:34:13,777
and take a look under the hood.

604
00:34:17,122 --> 00:34:18,283
Won't we?

605
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:20,487
Jim.

606
00:34:20,625 --> 00:34:22,355
Sorry, kid, it's just me.

607
00:34:27,532 --> 00:34:28,532
You all right?

608
00:34:29,100 --> 00:34:31,695
Yeah, I'm just, uh,
just looking for Jim.

609
00:34:31,836 --> 00:34:32,836
It's nothing.

610
00:34:33,471 --> 00:34:35,099
I saw soldiers downstairs.

611
00:34:36,274 --> 00:34:38,368
Yeah, the Army's finally
gotten off their asses

612
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:39,510
and decided to help.

613
00:34:39,611 --> 00:34:41,136
Jim's out with them now.

614
00:34:44,215 --> 00:34:45,547
Are you sure you're all right?

615
00:34:46,318 --> 00:34:48,310
(distant gunfire)

616
00:34:51,723 --> 00:34:52,782
I don't know.

617
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:58,091
I see people losing
their will to do good.

618
00:34:58,797 --> 00:35:00,288
People I love.

619
00:35:01,499 --> 00:35:02,939
What if we don't
make it out of this?

620
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:04,328
I'm not gonna lie, kid.

621
00:35:04,502 --> 00:35:08,405
These past few months,
I've wondered the same thing.

622
00:35:09,841 --> 00:35:11,118
And when I don't
know what to do,

623
00:35:11,142 --> 00:35:13,668
I come up here and I
dig into these case files.

624
00:35:14,512 --> 00:35:16,481
I sit my ass down
and I get to work.

625
00:35:17,582 --> 00:35:19,210
I used to hate this
kind of paperwork;

626
00:35:19,351 --> 00:35:21,071
now it's the only thing
that keeps me going.

627
00:35:21,486 --> 00:35:22,283
Why?

628
00:35:22,420 --> 00:35:24,514
Because the
little things matter.

629
00:35:24,656 --> 00:35:29,424
Act by act, deed by
deed, it means something.

630
00:35:30,261 --> 00:35:31,559
Even if no one notices

631
00:35:32,163 --> 00:35:33,163
or cares.

632
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:39,637
Thanks, Harvey.

633
00:35:39,671 --> 00:35:40,798
You're welcome, kid.

634
00:35:42,741 --> 00:35:44,869
If you really want to
do an old man a favor,

635
00:35:45,410 --> 00:35:47,845
you can scrounge me up
a cup of joe because I, uh...

636
00:35:52,884 --> 00:35:54,318
Kid's fast.

637
00:35:54,586 --> 00:35:56,612
(drill whirs)

638
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,156
I apologize for the discomfort.

639
00:35:59,758 --> 00:36:03,195
The neural cutout
inhibits muscular function,

640
00:36:03,762 --> 00:36:05,856
but not pain receptors.

641
00:36:06,431 --> 00:36:10,698
A simple reboot of the chip
should be all that is required.

642
00:36:10,835 --> 00:36:12,827
- Although, the sound may be...
- (drill whirring)

643
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:18,610
uh, somewhat unpleasant.
Not to mention the smell.

644
00:36:23,415 --> 00:36:25,247
(Edward groaning)

645
00:36:30,822 --> 00:36:32,313
(Edward snorts)

646
00:36:35,493 --> 00:36:36,517
(grunts)

647
00:36:58,750 --> 00:37:01,219
(Edward yips, growls)

648
00:37:07,459 --> 00:37:09,360
(Oswald panting)

649
00:37:09,494 --> 00:37:11,326
(Edward whines)

650
00:37:11,930 --> 00:37:12,930
(sighs)

651
00:37:16,301 --> 00:37:17,530
(inhales sharply)

652
00:37:17,702 --> 00:37:20,501
Edward, I believe
the time has come

653
00:37:20,638 --> 00:37:22,573
for a change of scenery.

654
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,500
(chuckles)

655
00:37:25,009 --> 00:37:28,241
It seems a powerful
electrical charge

656
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:32,509
overloaded your chip, but
I've gotten everything updated.

657
00:37:32,717 --> 00:37:36,313
I will pass the good news
along to your handler.

658
00:37:36,488 --> 00:37:37,683
(gun cocks)

659
00:37:37,822 --> 00:37:39,290
Care to expand on that?

660
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:44,525
I was merely helping a man
who needed medical attention.

661
00:37:44,796 --> 00:37:46,321
Yeah, not buying it.

662
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:50,768
His eyes are open.

663
00:37:50,902 --> 00:37:53,633
I gave him a
biomedical anesthesia.

664
00:37:53,772 --> 00:37:55,832
Wake him up now. Do it.

665
00:37:55,974 --> 00:37:58,307
Oh, very well.

666
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:02,572
(screams)

667
00:38:02,914 --> 00:38:03,914
Oh!

668
00:38:03,982 --> 00:38:05,814
I told you this wasn't me!

669
00:38:06,818 --> 00:38:08,411
He put a chip in my brain.

670
00:38:08,553 --> 00:38:10,579
And someone's been
controlling it this whole time.

671
00:38:10,755 --> 00:38:12,280
And then he drilled in my head!

672
00:38:12,590 --> 00:38:13,910
- Better talk now.
- (Nygma sighs)

673
00:38:13,992 --> 00:38:15,290
I am a scientist.

674
00:38:15,426 --> 00:38:19,864
A contract came along;
I developed a tool.

675
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:20,856
"A tool"?

676
00:38:21,032 --> 00:38:22,032
How dare you?

677
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:23,824
A contract from who?

678
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:31,332
Please escort the
professor out, thank you.

679
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:34,639
Ta-ta.

680
00:38:36,848 --> 00:38:37,941
What the hell is going on?

681
00:38:38,082 --> 00:38:41,883
Sorry, pal, but this part
of the op is need-to-know.

682
00:38:42,420 --> 00:38:44,465
I couldn't say anything until
we had the suspect in custody,

683
00:38:44,489 --> 00:38:47,425
but Walker wants Ed
Nygma taken out now.

684
00:38:49,093 --> 00:38:50,789
Walker was behind this?

685
00:38:51,396 --> 00:38:53,524
She's been controlling
Nygma the whole time?

686
00:38:54,465 --> 00:38:55,489
(scoffs)

687
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:57,826
You know I hate this spook crap.

688
00:38:57,969 --> 00:38:59,995
I don't ask questions;
I follow orders.

689
00:39:00,338 --> 00:39:01,966
She's responsible for Haven?

690
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:04,437
I don't understand, why...

691
00:39:04,576 --> 00:39:07,705
Jim, stop right there, trust me.

692
00:39:08,513 --> 00:39:11,574
Walker wants you to put a bullet

693
00:39:12,116 --> 00:39:13,379
in his brain.

694
00:39:17,121 --> 00:39:18,121
No.

695
00:39:18,656 --> 00:39:20,090
Call it proof of loyalty.

696
00:39:21,059 --> 00:39:23,927
It's what she needs from you
before she can move forward

697
00:39:24,062 --> 00:39:25,894
with final relief plans.

698
00:39:27,899 --> 00:39:29,060
Hey, come on.

699
00:39:29,667 --> 00:39:30,667
Look at him.

700
00:39:30,935 --> 00:39:31,935
He's a loon.

701
00:39:32,103 --> 00:39:33,503
A cop-killer.

702
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:36,965
Tell me the truth.

703
00:39:37,575 --> 00:39:39,840
Did Walker destroy
Haven? Did you know?

704
00:39:39,978 --> 00:39:42,641
- Tell me.
- Jim, ours is not
to reason why.

705
00:39:42,847 --> 00:39:45,908
And this is your chance
to be a part of this mission.

706
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:47,951
So...

707
00:39:49,721 --> 00:39:50,721
please.

708
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:53,585
You pull the trigger on him,

709
00:39:53,825 --> 00:39:55,418
or I pull the trigger on you.

710
00:39:57,695 --> 00:40:01,530
After all this, you'd kill
me for some bureaucrat?

711
00:40:02,867 --> 00:40:04,563
Mission comes first.

712
00:40:04,769 --> 00:40:05,793
You taught me that.

713
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:09,840
What's your answer?

714
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:28,620
Looks like I saved your
life one too many times.

715
00:40:32,730 --> 00:40:34,198
- Maybe so.
- (grunts)

716
00:40:34,832 --> 00:40:35,832
(Eduardo grunts)

717
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,641
You know Jim Gordon.

718
00:40:53,785 --> 00:40:54,809
You know this city.

719
00:40:55,053 --> 00:40:56,053
Find him.

720
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,120
And kill him.

721
00:41:08,666 --> 00:41:11,135
(hammering)

722
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,941
(scraping on stone)

723
00:41:22,747 --> 00:41:23,747
(gasps)

724
00:41:27,251 --> 00:41:28,947
Boss. Wake up.

725
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:31,581
Wake up.

726
00:41:31,923 --> 00:41:33,118
Ouch.

727
00:41:33,791 --> 00:41:36,488
Oh! Stitches still sore, huh?

728
00:41:37,095 --> 00:41:37,926
Never would have happened

729
00:41:38,062 --> 00:41:40,156
if you wore that
armor I prepared.

730
00:41:41,532 --> 00:41:44,593
That bullet is making
you sentimental.

731
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:48,036
Give her a shake, huh?

732
00:41:49,841 --> 00:41:52,504
Hmm. Better?

733
00:41:54,746 --> 00:41:58,012
I told you I had to let
Selina thrust the knife

734
00:41:58,149 --> 00:42:00,641
into my flesh at least once.

735
00:42:01,085 --> 00:42:03,953
Verisimilitude trumps
precaution, you see.

736
00:42:04,255 --> 00:42:05,255
I get it.

737
00:42:05,556 --> 00:42:07,821
Selina Kyle and Bruce
Wayne needed to think

738
00:42:07,959 --> 00:42:09,086
you were dead, boss.

739
00:42:09,227 --> 00:42:12,527
Yeah. Right.

740
00:42:12,663 --> 00:42:13,663
(gasps)

741
00:42:13,865 --> 00:42:15,527
I take it you have news?

742
00:42:16,034 --> 00:42:17,696
All systems go.

743
00:42:17,835 --> 00:42:19,701
- Well, then lead the way.
- Oh!

744
00:42:34,585 --> 00:42:35,609
Doctor.

745
00:42:36,054 --> 00:42:37,852
I'm hearing good things.

746
00:42:38,122 --> 00:42:39,920
The bandages are
ready to come off.

747
00:42:40,691 --> 00:42:42,887
Your assistant thought
you'd like to see the results.

748
00:42:44,295 --> 00:42:45,729
Indeed, I would.

749
00:42:59,944 --> 00:43:01,310
(laughs)

750
00:43:04,348 --> 00:43:07,944
Oh, you two look beautiful.

751
00:43:10,321 --> 00:43:12,085
Oh...

752
00:43:13,724 --> 00:43:17,957
I love family
reunions, don't you?
